14. A New Training Architecture

We propose a seven-stage architecture.

Stage 1 — Observation

Raw data enters the system.

X\rightarrow \text{observations}

Stage 2 — Felectronization

Observations are converted into candidate Felectron states.

X\rightarrow\mathrm{ƒe}

Stage 3 — Relation Discovery

The system searches for relationships between Felectrons.

\mathrm{ƒe}_i\rightarrow\mathrm{ƒe}_j

Stage 4 — Category Formation

Related Felectrons form categorical structures.

\{\mathrm{ƒe}\}\rightarrow\mathcal C

Stage 5 — Functorial Abstraction

The system identifies structure-preserving transformations between categories.

F:\mathcal C\rightarrow\mathcal M

Stage 6 — Composition

Known structures are composed to generate new predictions.

f,g\rightarrow g\circ f

Stage 7 — Field Stabilization

Useful structures become stable Felectron configurations while redundant information decays.

