15. Architecture of a Felectron Learning Machine

A hypothetical Felectron Learning system would contain:

1. Observation Layer

Receives sensory or symbolic data.

2. Felectron Encoder

Extracts candidate units of information.

3. Morphism Engine

Discovers relationships.

4. Categorical Memory

Stores concepts and their structural relationships.

5. Composition Engine

Generates new knowledge through compositional inference.

6. Felectron Field

Maintains distributed contextual information.

7. Prediction Engine

Uses the resulting categorical structure to predict future states.

This architecture could coexist with neural networks.

For example:

\text{Neural Network}
+
\text{Categorical Reasoning}
+
\text{Felectron Dynamics}

could form a hybrid system.

