17. Few-Shot Learning as the Natural Test Case

Felectron Learning makes a particularly strong prediction:

Systems explicitly optimized for categorical structure should perform better with limited training examples when the underlying domain contains compositional regularities.

Therefore, evaluation should emphasize:

* 1-shot learning,
* 5-shot learning,
* 10-shot learning,
* small-data classification,
* compositional generalization,
* out-of-distribution generalization,
* systematic extrapolation.

The central experiment is not:

\text{Does more data improve performance?}

It is:

\boxed{
\text{Can the same performance be achieved with dramatically less data?}
}

