Felectron Learning makes a deliberately ambitious hypothesis:

A sufficiently capable learner should require fewer examples when it learns the algebra of relationships underlying a domain rather than merely fitting the statistical distribution of its examples.

This is not currently an established scientific fact.

It is the central hypothesis to be tested.

