22. The Felectron Learning Principle

We therefore propose the following foundational principle:

The Intelligence Efficiency Principle: An artificial learner becomes more data-efficient as it increasingly represents reusable relational structure rather than independent observations.

This suggests:

\text{Data Efficiency}
\propto
\frac{\text{Reusable Structure}}
{\text{Redundant Information}}

The objective of future machine-learning systems should consequently shift from:

\boxed{\text{Scale Everything}}

toward:

\boxed{\text{Discover Structure}}

